From 3e40927fc6e42a55bebc80d888232c0b52ea8607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:35:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?reaper=20v2.0.0:=20security-hardening=20batch?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20(AUDIT-1=20=C2=A72=20+=20AUDIT-2=20follow-ups)=20-=20no=20ve?=
 =?UTF-8?q?rsion=20change?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Addresses the open hardening items from both audits. Version stays Reaper_v2.0.0 (in-place re-spin).

A2-SEC-001/002 (libcodb/cosql_utils.c): value literals now use sqlite3_snprintf %Q (self-quoting,
  escapes embedded ') at 24 TEXT/MAC/IP/JSON sinks (gen_match/gen_upsert/insert); 7 identifier
  sinks now validated with the existing is_valid_sql_identifier (column names, ORDER BY, WHERE
  column in remove/backup_and_remove). Internal fixed ATTACH path + legit multi-column backup
  list deliberately left (flagged).
A1-SEC-002 (httpd/web.c + Reaper_Diag/Warden.asp): the two read CGIs that popen() a subprocess
  (do_reaper_diag_cgi, do_reaper_warden_cgi) now require the http_id CSRF token; both frontend
  GETs now send it. Verified these CGIs have no other callers.
A4-UI-001/002/003 (Reaper_Devices/Storage/Wireless/reaper_shell): esc() unified to encode " and '
  (attribute-safe); chanspec and menuTree name/url encoded before innerHTML/document.write.
B6 (inherited www): htmlEncode the DHCP-hostname/nvram name class in the remaining sinks -
  OpenVPN server CN+username + client desc + WireGuard peer name (Advanced_VPNStatus.asp),
  AiMesh node/client names (aimesh_topology.html), USB disk name (disk.asp) + folder-tree
  text/title (disk_functions.js). Model-name/log-key/IP-column paths checked and left (not
  LAN-client data or already encoded).
B5-SEC-001 (mssl/mssl.c): the CLIENT TLS path now loads the shipped CA bundle
  (/rom/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt), sets SSL_VERIFY_PEER + hostname verification
  (SSL_set1_host), and FAILS CLOSED if no CA is available. Server path unchanged (keeps
  SSL_VERIFY_NONE). The mssl client path currently has NO callers (httpd + rmcpd use mssl as
  SERVER only; DDNS/feeds use curl), so this is latent-path defense-in-depth with zero
  field-connectivity impact; rmcpd (MCP) is server-only and unaffected.
A4-UI-004: no change - the qos.c consumer already re-validates (bandwidth bail/clamp +
  validate_apply_input_value on qos_bw_rulelist).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
